  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Show that each of the following functions are not surjective:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p25-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f:\\mathbb{N}\\to\\mathbb{N}$ where $f(n)=n+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1$ is not in the range, so $f$ is not surjective.",
          "worked": "For every $n\\in\\mathbb{N}$, $n\\ge 1$, so $f(n)=n+1\\ge 2$. Thus $1\\in\\mathbb{N}$ has no preimage, and $f$ is not surjective.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f:\\mathbb{Z}\\to\\mathbb{Z}$ where $f(n)=2n+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2$ is not in the range, so $f$ is not surjective.",
          "worked": "If $f(n)=2$, then\n$$\\begin{align*}2n+1&=2\\\\2n&=1\\\\n&=\\tfrac12.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\tfrac12\\notin\\mathbb{Z}$, the codomain value $2$ has no preimage. Therefore, $f$ is not surjective.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f:\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}$ where $f(x)=x^4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-1$ is not in the range, so $f$ is not surjective.",
          "worked": "For every real $x$, $f(x)=x^4\\ge 0$. Thus $-1\\in\\mathbb{R}$ has no preimage, and $f$ is not surjective.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q7-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$f:\\mathbb{R}^{+}\\to\\mathbb{R}^{+}$ where $f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{x+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2$ is not in the range, so $f$ is not surjective.",
          "worked": "For $x>0$, we have $x+1>1$, so $0<f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{x+1}<1$. Thus $2\\in\\mathbb{R}^{+}$ has no preimage, and $f$ is not surjective.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 19
      }
    ]
  },
